==Swedish==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gml|sv}} {{term|kort|lang=gml}}. Cognate with German {{term|kurz|lang=de}}, Danish {{term|kort|lang=da}} and Norwegian {{term|kort|lang=no}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{audio|Sv-kort.ogg|audio}}

====Adjective====
{{sv-adj-reg|n=kort}}
'''kort'''

# [[short]]

=====Antonyms=====
* [[lång]]

=====Derived terms=====
* [[korthet]]
* [[kortbyxor]]

=====Quotations=====
* '''1901''', [http://runeberg.org/topnovel/b0313.html ''Noveller''] av [[w:Zacharias Topelius|Zacharias Topelius]] - Thomas! Thomas! [...]viskade nu Lotten, ty det var den '''korte''' som segrat, och hon hade igenkänt honom.
*: Thomas! Thomas! Lotten now whispered, since it was the short one that had won, and she had recognized him.
* '''1931''', [http://runeberg.org/clownjac/05.html ''Clownen Jac''] av [[w:Hjalmar Bergman|Hjalmar Bergman]] - '''Kortaste''' avståndet mellan två punkter är den krokiga linjen, ju krokigare, desto '''kortare'''.
*: The shortest distance between two points is the crooked line, the more crooked, the shorter.

===Etymology 2===
Probably from {{etyl|da|sv}} {{term|kort|lang=da}} or {{etyl|gml|sv}} {{term|kort|lang=gml}}.

====Noun====
{{sv-decl-noun|gender=Neuter|kort|kortet|kort|korten|korts|kortets|korts|kortens}}
'''kort'''

# [[card]]; a piece of stiff paper or plastic.
# [[playing card]]
# game involving playing cards
#: ''Ska vi spela '''kort'''?'' = ''Shall we play cards?''
# [[photograph]]

